A||||6||The Fieromaster||Fieromaster88's V6 convert!||||10||
Z||000000||The Fieromaster||07-07-2001||11:38 PM||||Well FINALLY we have finished Fieromaster88's v6 conversion on his 88 Fiero Coupe (38,000 miles)!  Goodbye slow 4 banger hello 2.8 with Isuzu 5 speed!  The conversion went good... ran into a FEW! problems...  The extent was the auto to manual conversion (new 79$ clutch line) and the fact that the slave wouldnt push in far enough so we had to modify a bracket... hehe - I love my welder!!  Oh yes yes the lack of preperation was a big one... woopsie!  Sorry again James!  Well all in all James is on his way home and I am calling him like every 30 minutes to see how he is doing!  Last time I talked to him he said he loves his car and he keeps slowing down only to drop a gear and stomp it!<BR>Lots of parts stollin from my GT though to make his car go...  Here is a few things you might want to get before this conversion...<BR>4 or 5 speed tranny mounts<BR>Dog bone<BR>Intake setup<BR>Computer<BR>Any lines you may need (clutch or hoses for coolant)<BR>Shifter cables<BR>slave or master cylender (spelling?)<BR>We used the clutch from my 4 speed 85 Fiero GT (not sure if it is right for conversion, this may be cause or our need for custom slave mounts)<BR>The release bearing has to be the one from the isuzu though cause it connects in all weird!<BR>Well if i remember anything else ill post it... I know i did!  Damn it... cant remember what else I was gonna say!  Well anyway its been like 6 or 7 days on his car so its time to relax... later all!<P>Peace!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||10
